WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.647
Granite peaks, limestone plateaux, and the monsoon.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.488
The Haggeher mountains rise to about fifteen hundred metres above the north coast,

00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:11.468
their granite peaks often in cloud.

00:00:12.568 --> 00:00:16.677
Below them, limestone plateaux are riddled with sinkholes and caves.

00:00:16.677 --> 00:00:21.271
Hoq Cave, on the north coast, holds inscriptions left by sailors from India,

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.990
southern Arabia, Ethiopia, Greece and beyond,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.556
mostly from the first to sixth centuries of the common era.

00:00:28.656 --> 00:00:32.502
On the south coast, broad plains and dunes run down to the sea.

00:00:32.502 --> 00:00:37.507
From June to September the south-west monsoon brings gale-force winds that cut the

00:00:37.507 --> 00:00:38.606
island off by sea.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:43.089
The monsoon also brings mist and low cloud to the uplands.

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:46.997
The umbrella-shaped dragon's blood trees comb water from that mist,

00:00:46.997 --> 00:00:49.447
a process called horizontal precipitation.
